{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "id": "muradin",
  "name": "Muradin",
  "role": "Tank",
  "overview": "Muradin is a generalist Tank that excels at disrupting the enemy team, dealing damage, and surviving kill attempts. His versatile kit allows him to do many things, from peeling to diving, from scouting to ganking.\n\nDuring the laning phase, he can focus on giving vision as well as messing up enemy rotations by dismounting and chunking down enemy Heroes. Dwarf Toss allows him to easily escape from most situations. Second Wind denies all damage he received. Meanwhile, he farms stack for his Baseline Quest which empowers Storm Bolt.\n\nDuring team fights, he can either play defensively or offensively. The choice depends on the situation, your team composition, and the enemy team composition. When playing defensively, he mainly focuses on peeling and/or counter-engaging for his team. When playing offensively, he primarily focuses on engaging and/or diving vulnerable enemy Heroes.",
  "strengths": [
    "Strong self-sustain",
    "Decent crowd control",
    "Good mobility"
  ],
  "weaknesses": [
    "Not able to peel from high mobility Heroes (like Tracer)",
    "Weak to crowd control that can stop Dwarf Toss"
  ],
